    G2.5: (1) the data-repository contract listed entities that are not in
    v0; (2) the localstorage-migration adapter overclaimed "idempotent" while
    re-stamping updatedAt on every rerun, which would have produced
    spurious sync-conflict signals; (3) the tauri-commands contract claimed
    "every JS-callable command has a runtime ensure_*_allowed check" but
    window.rs and menubar.rs still lacked one. Close the gaps so the
    contracts and the runtime tell the same story.
    
    What:
    C1 — Move productivity.pomodoro_session / widgets.widget / account.device
    out of the §2 frozen entity table into a new §2.1 "Deferred future
    entities" subsection. Replace `pending commit` with `744d578` in the
    repository-v0-contract dev_log work-log.
    
    C2 — Tighten organizer-layout-migration. Before re-`put`-ing a record
    the migration now reads the existing record via `repo.get` and skips
    the put when all meaningful fields (excluding `createdAt` / `updatedAt`)
    match. Add a new `unchanged` counter to OrganizerLayoutMigrationResult,
    and pre-seed `skipped` to 0 so P1-Alpha's A3 empty-filepath skip can
    land independently without merge conflicts. Update the existing
    idempotency test to expect `unchanged: 4` instead of re-migrated
    counts, and add a dedicated test proving rerun does not change
    `updatedAt`. Update localstorage-migration dev_log to describe the new
    precise behaviour and drop the bare "idempotent" word.
    
    C3 — Extend the runtime allow-list pattern to window.rs and menubar.rs.
    Add `WINDOW_ALLOWED_WINDOWS = ["main", "control"]` and
    `ensure_window_command_allowed(label)`; inject `window: WebviewWindow`
    into the 5 window lifecycle commands so the IPC layer auto-extracts the
    caller window (JS-side invoke signatures unchanged). Refactor the
    internal create→update fallback into `update_grid_window_internal` so
    `create_grid_window` does not re-trigger the public allow-list check
    after it has already passed. Add `MENUBAR_ALLOWED_WINDOWS =
    ["control", "main"]` and `ensure_menubar_window_allowed(label)` and
    gate `sync_set_menubar_status`. Add cargo unit tests
    `window_allowlist_admits_main_control` /
    `window_allowlist_rejects_grid_widget` and
    `menubar_allowlist_admits_control_main` /
    `menubar_allowlist_rejects_other`.
    
    Scope:
    - docs/contracts/data-repository-v0.md
    - docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md
    - packages/repository-v0-contract/docs/dev_log.md
    - packages/localstorage-migration/docs/dev_log.md
    - packages/core-data/src/organizer-layout-migration.ts
    - packages/core-data/tests/organizer-layout-migration.test.ts
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/window.rs
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/menubar.rs
    - apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/AUDIT.md
    
    Risk:
    - C2 changes the `OrganizerLayoutMigrationResult` shape; only consumer
      is the test suite (re-export from `@repo/core-data` is unchanged at
      the type level — new fields are additive).
    - C3 adds an extra positional `window: WebviewWindow` parameter to
      6 Tauri commands. Tauri injects this automatically — JS callers
      (`apps/desktop/src/...`, `packages/plugin-organizer/...`) do not
      change their invoke signatures. Verified by reading
      `useGridWindow.ts`, `useSyncMenuBarStatus.ts`, and `ControlWindow.tsx`.
    - C3 reduces effective callers of `update_grid_window` /
      `close_grid_window` from `main`+`control`+`grid_*` down to
      `main`+`control`. The doc previously said `grid_*` was allowed but
      there is no actual `grid_*` caller in the codebase today; grid
      windows route through `control` via cross-window events.
    
    Docs:
    - §2.1 deferred-entity subsection added to the data-repository contract.
