    53	G1.1 implementation notes:
    54	
    55	- Rust is the only label generation point via `grid_{gridId}`.
    56	- Invalid `gridId` values return `INVALID_GRID_ID`.
    57	- Missing windows return `WINDOW_NOT_FOUND`.
    58	- Native window failures return `WINDOW_NATIVE_ERROR`.
    59	- Runtime allow-list `commands::window::WINDOW_ALLOWED_WINDOWS`
    60	  (`main`, `control`) enforces the table above at the IPC boundary
    61	  with `WINDOW_CAPABILITY_DENIED`. `grid_*` windows are intentionally
    62	  excluded — a grid window must request lifecycle changes for itself
    63	  via cross-window events routed through `control`, not by directly
    64	  invoking `update_grid_window` / `close_grid_window` against another
    65	  grid. Widget / pet / ai-cube / console are likewise rejected.
    66	- The `window: tauri::WebviewWindow` argument is injected by the
    67	  Tauri IPC layer; JS callers do NOT include it in the args payload
    68	  (mirrors the crypto / database / keychain command pattern).
