   187	|---|---|
   188	| `default.json` | main/control/grid baseline window capability |
   189	| `plugin-account-crypto.json` | account/control crypto marker + command-side allowlist |
   190	| `plugin-account-keychain.json` | account/control keychain marker + command-side allowlist |
   191	| `plugin-data-database.json` | main/control/grid/account/console Repository v0 marker + runtime allowlist (G2.5) |
   192	
   193	Full audit table: `apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/AUDIT.md`.
   194	
   195	G2.5 invariants now enforced:
   196	
   197	- Every JS-callable command has a capability file declaring its allowed
   198	  windows.
   199	- The following command groups carry a runtime
   200	  `ensure_*_allowed(label)` defence-in-depth check that mirrors the
   201	  capability file scope, so widget / pet / ai-cube windows cannot
   202	  invoke them even if a future capability file widening lands by
   203	  mistake:
   204	
   205	  | Command group | Runtime allow-list constant | Source |
   206	  |---|---|---|
   207	  | `crypto_*` | `CRYPTO_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` | `commands/crypto.rs` |
   208	  | `secret_*` | `KEYCHAIN_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` | `commands/keychain.rs` |
   209	  | `db_*` | `DATABASE_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` | `commands/database.rs` |
   210	  | `reveal_in_finder`, `open_path` | `FINDER_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` | `commands/finder.rs` |
   211	  | `create_grid_window`, `update_grid_window`, `close_grid_window`, `list_grid_windows`, `focus_grid_window` | `WINDOW_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` | `commands/window.rs` |
   212	  | `sync_set_menubar_status` | `MENUBAR_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` | `commands/menubar.rs` |
   213	
   214	  Other commands (`clipboard_*`, etc.) currently rely on capability
   215	  file scope alone — their runtime allow-lists are tracked under
   216	  future hardening rows and not in v0.
